{"name":"Fairy Tail","hex":"#ecdde5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fairy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical being of human form with magical powers, known in many sizes and descriptions, although typically depicted as a small sprite with gauze-like wings, especially one that is female. Fairies are revered in some modern forms of paganism.","A male homosexual, especially one who is effeminate."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Like a fairy; fanciful, whimsical, delicate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy"},{"term":"tail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The caudal appendage of an animal that is attached to their posterior and near the anus or cloaca.","An object or part of an object resembling a tail in shape, such as the thongs on a cat-o'-nine-tails; a strand of material hanging from something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hold by the end; said of a timber when it rests upon a wall or other support; with in or into","To swing with the stern in a certain direction; said of a vessel at anchor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fairy Tail","blocks":[{"text":"Fairy Tail is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Hiro Mashima. It was serialized in Kodansha's Weekly Shōnen Magazine from August 2006 to July 2017, with the individual chapters collected and published into 63 tankōbon volumes. The story follows the adventures of Natsu Dragneel, a member of the popular wizard guild Fairy Tail, as he searches the fictional world of Earth-land for the dragon Igneel."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/FairyTail-Volume_1_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy_Tail","wikidata":"Q18796"},{"title":"Fairy Tail (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Fairy Tail is a Japanese anime television series produced by A-1 Pictures, Dentsu, Satelight, Bridge, and CloverWorks. Based on the manga series Fairy Tail by Hiro Mashima, the series aired for 328 episodes on TV Tokyo and its TXN affiliates from October 12, 2009, to September 29, 2019. The series follows the journeys of Natsu Dragneel, Lucy Heartfilia and the wizard guild, Fairy Tail. A sequel series, titled Fairy Tail: 100 Years Quest, aired from July 2024 to January 2025."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy_Tail_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q16510277"},{"title":"Fairy","blocks":[{"text":"A fairy is a type of mythical being or legendary creature, generally described as anthropomorphic, found in the folklore of multiple European cultures, a form of spirit, often with magical, metaphysical, supernatural, or preternatural qualities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg/330px-Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy","wikidata":"Q8028"},{"title":"Tail","blocks":[{"text":"The tail is the elongated section at the rear end of a bilaterian animal's body; in general, the term refers to a distinct, flexible appendage extending backwards from the midline of the torso. In vertebrate animals that evolved to lose their tails, the coccyx is the homologous vestigial of the tail. While tails are primarily considered a feature of vertebrates, some invertebrates such as scorpions and springtails, as well as snails and slugs, have tail-like appendages that are also referred to as tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg/330px-White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tail","wikidata":"Q60960"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Hiro_Mashima_-_Japan_Expo_2010_-_Day3_-_P1460393.jpg/500px-Hiro_Mashima_-_Japan_Expo_2010_-_Day3_-_P1460393.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Hiro_Mashima_-_Japan_Expo_2010_-_Day3_-_P1460393.jpg/1280px-Hiro_Mashima_-_Japan_Expo_2010_-_Day3_-_P1460393.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Hiro_Mashima_-_Japan_Expo_2010_-_Day3_-_P1460393.jpg/500px-Hiro_Mashima_-_Japan_Expo_2010_-_Day3_-_P1460393.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Author and illustrator Hiro Mashima","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHiro_Mashima_-_Japan_Expo_2010_-_Day3_-_P1460393.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/10.16.1FairyTailCastByLuigiNovi4.jpg/500px-10.16.1FairyTailCastByLuigiNovi4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/10.16.1FairyTailCastByLuigiNovi4.jpg/1280px-10.16.1FairyTailCastByLuigiNovi4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/10.16.1FairyTailCastByLuigiNovi4.jpg/500px-10.16.1FairyTailCastByLuigiNovi4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Funimation staff and voice cast of the anime at the 2011 New York Comic Con, from left to right: Todd Haberkorn (Natsu), Cherami Leigh (Lucy), Colleen Clinkenbeard (Erza), Newton Pittman (Gray), and Tyler Walker (ADR director).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A10.16.1FairyTailCastByLuigiNovi4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg/500px-James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg?u